Subject: [PATCH] Nest a lone empty bullet instead of setext-heading the line
 above

In the Notes markdown preview a list item followed by an empty nested
bullet turned the parent's text into an <h2> (issue #517):

  - 1
    -

CommonMark reads the lone `-` as a setext-heading underline for the
paragraph above it, so markdown-it's `lheading` rule claims it before the
`list` rule runs. Even without `lheading`, `list` refuses to let an empty
bullet interrupt a paragraph, so it degrades to lazy `1<br>-` text.

Add a notes-preview markdown-it plugin that treats a lone single `-` as an
empty bullet, not a setext underline, and lets an empty bullet interrupt a
paragraph so it nests as an empty child item. Multi-dash `---` and `=`
setext headings are untouched.

